          "id": "prt_msg_ses_44_06_03",
          "sessionID": "ses_44",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_44_06",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A test that only sometimes fails almost always points to a real bug — a race condition, an unawaited promise, a timing-dependent assertion — not bad luck. Rerunning until it passes just hides that and ships the bug. The failure here is a DB connection timeout, which suggests the test starts before the test DB is ready; worth fixing that instead of retrying."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_msg_ses_44_06_04",
          "sessionID": "ses_44",
